WEBVTT

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:13.720
It won't stop.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.350
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.810
Guys, what's happening on your screens?
Any changes?

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.680
Mine says there's been an error.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:25.020
-Mine too.
-Same here.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.110
That means this fourth booth is
the only one not working right.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.440
I'm going to reboot it.
Let's try it one more time.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:03.990
PURE BRIGHTNESS

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.330
All right, I'll countdown from five again.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:07.710
Five.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:08.710
<i>Four.</i>

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:09.710
<i>Three.</i>

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:10.710
<i>Two.</i>

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:11.710
<i>One.</i>

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:12.750
<i>Zero.</i>

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.960
WOULD YOU LIKE TO CANCEL THE FINAL ORDER?
YES

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:16.880
No good.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:23.100
Guys, my terminal here is busted
and can't seem to cancel the order.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:25.060
You're kidding.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.520
After all that work.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.940
We ended up wasting a lot of time.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:30.440
Come back, everyone.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:32.400
We need to meet up where Hotaru is.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.570
<i>Well, I wouldn't call it all a waste.</i>

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:39.990
<i>I thought this ship was just
a hunk of creepy and disgusting metal.</i>

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:43.030
<i>But we found out that people lived here
and ate curry and stuff.</i>

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.660
<i>I realized they led
perfectly normal lives here.</i>

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:48.710
I started to think it was homey, in a way.

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:49.910
<i>"Homey"?</i>

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:52.580
Sort of charming, you know.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.290
I don't understand.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.550
Which part of that
doesn't make this a waste of time?

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.170
Well, he has a point.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.140
It was ordinary folks who pushed
the switch to launch the missiles

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.600
<i>after going through a lot.</i>

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.770
Guys, turn off the power
to your terminals.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:10.350
Oh, hey, Hotaru.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.150
Do you think we can
cut the ship's main power source?

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:14.980
Like maybe by stopping the engines.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.900
<i>If we stop whatever generates power,</i>

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.450
<i>then the missiles
won't be able to launch, right?</i>

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.530
I'll do some checking.

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:25.530
I'll head for the engine room
and see if I can stop them.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.910
Oh, we're going to break stuff?
Count me in!

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:29.910
I'll join you too!

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:33.420
The bacteria?

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:35.630
How did so much get here?

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.920
I have to be careful not to touch it.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:42.470
I should pass through the other side.

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:45.760
Have you figured anything out, Hotaru?

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:48.680
Ango, it seems it might not be possible.

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.560
I can't access the schematics
or wiring blueprints

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:54.150
without an ID and password.

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.230
I see.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:58.230
<i>I don't know anything about computers.</i>

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:02.990
<i>We were taught almost nothing
about how generators or engines work.</i>

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:04.950
Arashi?

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.740
I'm sorry. I can't figure it out.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:11.040
But I know the bottom level
is considered a restricted area,

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:12.910
so something important
might be down there.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.330
<i>Roger that. Thanks.</i>

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:18.540
<i>I don't think I would have ever found
that code we were looking for earlier.</i>

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:21.210
<i>Ango, you there? Too bad it didn't work.</i>

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:24.470
Is that you, Ryo? Yes.
How are things on your end?

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:27.470
We've had no luck either.
We can't find an exit.

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:30.640
All the routes we came in from
have been shut off by thick walls.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:34.770
It seems we can't just leave normally.
We'll search for another way.

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:38.270
Don't you think it was all a waste, Ryo,

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:40.280
what we learned back then?

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:42.150
I'll contact you later.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:45.780
It sounded like Ango was
feeling really down.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:47.820
I'm feeling down too.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.950
I was enjoying thinking about curry
until just a little while ago.

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:54.330
Hey, Ryo. What kind of curry did you like?

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:56.420
I don't have any preferences
regarding food.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:59.420
What? Does that mean
there's nothing you like?

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:01.130
I don't care, as long as it's edible.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.710
That's crazy.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.470
What about your preferences
regarding people?

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.470
Do you have any preferences
regarding people similar to me?

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:11.510
Similar to what about you?

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.390
Well, I mean, people
who are always spunky and happy,

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.850
who are petite, cute,
and have a bit of a curl.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:18.980
"Curl"?

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:22.940
Naturally curly hair.
Like frizzy, and with big, round eyes--

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:27.160
I see. I think people who are spunky
and have curly hair are fine.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.450
Is that right?

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.790
<i>I meant that in a positive way.</i>

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.160
<i>He already knows someone like that.</i>

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:38.830
<i>Someone spunky and with curly hair.</i>

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:42.590
<i>And he was thinking about
that person just now.</i>

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.550
<i>It's such a shock
that even I'm surprised by it.</i>

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:48.510
<i>Oh, to be young.</i>

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:51.180
<i>We're still below sea level.</i>

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.890
<i>And the ship won't let us go any higher.</i>

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.270
<i>We can't get out by opening holes
in the wall.</i>

00:05:57.770 --> 00:06:01.610
<i>I don't want to set off an explosion
since it may disturb the hull's balance.</i>

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:07.240
Since the ship turned vertical,
then the missiles must come out the top.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.700
That's it, Matsuri! Nice thinking!

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:14.990
Ango, there should be an exit we can use.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.750
I'm going to check, so just wait.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.080
"There should be"?

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:19.120
And also,

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:22.340
Matsuri, do you still feel like
it was worth coming here?

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:23.290
Yes!

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:28.050
<i>I mean, Ryo and I are totally closer
than before we came here.</i>

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:29.050
You heard her.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:32.100
Ango, the only way to waste time is
by thinking of it as a waste.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:34.600
<i>What matters is how you feel about it.</i>

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:35.640
What?

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:36.850
<i>I'll contact you again later.</i>

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:37.930
Wait, Ryo.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.390
<i>How I feel about it?</i>

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:42.810
<i>When did Ryo start saying
ambiguous things like that?</i>

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.190
Hey!

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.320
We're in big trouble!

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.030
Didn't you go below
to meet up with Arashi and Natsu?

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:49.650
I couldn't find a way!

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:52.990
<i>All of a sudden, everything is
rusted over and falling apart.</i>

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:54.990
<i>The ladders are falling apart too!</i>

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.160
What are we going to do?

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:58.250
Arashi and Natsu won't be
able to get back up!

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:02.130
<i>I don't know how this works,
but I'm turning them all off.</i>

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.630
<i>Stop. Please stop.</i>

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:10.050
<i>If the missiles launch
and land where Hana is, then...</i>

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:12.300
<i>Stop! Just stop!</i>

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:16.140
<i>It feels like something is chasing me.</i>

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:17.640
<i>Could it be...</i>

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:24.690
-Natsu?
-Arashi!

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:27.610
What's wrong?

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:30.030
I'm fine. Let me help you.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:32.160
Okay. Let's turn everything off.

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:34.740
We can't go this way.

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:38.240
See what I mean? The B and C blocks
are even worse than this.

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.790
Will they even be able
to make it back here?

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.790
Let's see where we can pull them up
over the shortest distance by rope.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:46.210
You and Ryo sure are amazing.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:47.250
Why is that?

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:50.630
You're quick to decide what to do next
and then immediately act on it.

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:52.180
That's just natural.

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:56.010
It's not natural.

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:58.350
<i>Considering the location,
this should be the door.</i>

00:07:58.430 --> 00:07:59.680
What? What's this?

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:01.390
When we were on the elevator,

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:03.980
I saw something on the left
that looked like a ladder.

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:08.360
The missiles going up that hole there?

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.860
Yes. It was really noisy.

00:08:14.070 --> 00:08:15.030
We'll climb up here.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:19.370
There should be a hatch up here
for the missiles to launch through.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:22.040
And that's our exit.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:24.920
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.460
<i>Arashi, are you okay?</i>

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:28.210
Yes. Natsu is with me.

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:30.510
But Semimaru hasn't shown up yet.

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:31.800
<i>I couldn't make it.</i>

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:33.380
-What?
-Listen up.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:36.260
The bacteria suddenly started
propagating like mad.

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:39.640
The paths connecting us to you
are now impassible on every block.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.480
You mean we can't go back the way we came?

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:45.810
<i>Exactly. We're having Hotaru
search for alternate routes now.</i>

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:48.560
<i>You still okay, Natsu?
Not scared out of your wits?</i>

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:49.900
I'm just fine.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:51.980
Even when I was searching for
the code alone,

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:54.570
it was strange,
but I wasn't scared at all.

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:56.570
<i>Oh, really? You're sounding tough.</i>

00:08:56.660 --> 00:09:01.490
Natsu, if you feel fine
in a situation like this, doubt yourself.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:04.330
<i>You're not in a proper state of mind.</i>

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:06.920
<i>Humans get careless
when they're riding a high.</i>

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.130
Fear is natural. Embrace the anxiety.

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:12.590
It's precisely what keeps you cautious
and aware. Got it?

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:16.050
<i>Trust yourself,
but always keep in mind your doubts.</i>

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:17.430
Okay.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:19.180
<i>This is more complicated than I thought.</i>

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:21.220
<i>I still have a lot to work on.</i>

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:24.310
Say, Ango,
how did you learn all this stuff?

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:26.230
Simply through experience.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:29.150
<i>Arashi and Ango, can you both hear me?</i>

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:30.060
<i>I hear you.</i>

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:32.650
Arashi, it looks like
you're at the bottom of A block.

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:36.990
If you go to the side opposite the hallway
all the way to the end,

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:39.910
you'll find a vertical passageway,
like a ventilation shaft.

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:41.410
Go out that way.

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:45.160
<i>Ango, are you able to reach A-3-15
from where you are?</i>

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:48.120
Yes,
I think it's still possible to get there.

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:49.670
Roger. We'll go and see.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:52.380
<i>We'll rendezvous there, Arashi. Hurry.</i>

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:55.170
<i>Arashi, did you copy that?</i>

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:59.640
Ango, I'm going to stay here until
the last minute to shut this thing down.

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:02.470
We've already cut it too close.
We need time to escape.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:05.350
Look, I want to stop these missiles
no matter what it takes.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:08.560
I'll make sure Natsu gets there.
Bring her up first.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.940
If you just leave the rope,
then I'll follow later.

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:12.860
Arashi!

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:14.820
I must stop the--

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:19.910
<i>What happened?</i>

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:21.280
Natsu!

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:25.450
Hurry! Get outside!

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:28.790
Those things went straight for the blood.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:33.000
It looked like they were also after you.
Did you get injured or something?

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:35.880
I'm not injured, but...

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:38.340
Well, I...

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:40.760
I'm on my period.

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:42.390
Sorry.

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:43.760
But I get it now.

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:46.720
Those things don't necessarily
attack humans,

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:48.350
but they're attracted to blood.

00:10:48.430 --> 00:10:49.730
You're kidding!

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:53.610
<i>When I threw that garbage away
in the bathroom earlier,</i>

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:56.110
<i>it must have gotten a taste for blood.</i>

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:57.280
<i>That must be it.</i>

00:10:57.360 --> 00:10:58.610
Crap. Let's move!

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:01.240
Ango, we're headed to
the rendezvous point.

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:02.740
The bacteria are attacking!

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:04.120
-What did you say?
-What?

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:14.750
It's an exit,
but it's also the launch port.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.000
That means the preparations are
proceeding steadily.

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:18.920
<i>What do you mean
the bacteria are attacking?</i>

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:20.470
<i>Hey! Say something, Natsu!</i>

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:23.640
It sounds like the others are
having problems of their own.

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:24.640
Right.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:27.390
Ryo, come back!

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:30.520
I will, after I secure our escape route
down the outside.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:33.440
Just come back!
We'll handle the rest from here.

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:35.360
Meet up with Ango.

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:37.360
It seems like Arashi and Natsu
are in trouble.

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:39.110
Go and help them.

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:40.440
You can do that, right?

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:42.200
Roger that.

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.200
Take this with you.

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:45.160
Okay.

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:46.490
You're staying here, Matsuri.

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:47.580
Seriously?

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:50.660
See you.

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:52.460
Ryo, please be careful!

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.880
I'm worried since I can't be with you.

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:07.560
It's just past that door!

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:09.220
Ango, what's going on?

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:11.430
The bacteria can attack people?

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:16.650
They're down here. Semimaru, help me out.

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:20.940
What? Down here? Are we pulling them up?

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:24.110
But how? I'm not strong enough to do that.

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:26.200
This should just barely reach them.

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:29.790
Arashi! Natsu!

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:31.370
Ango!

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:33.580
We'll pull you both up quickly!

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:34.540
How?

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.210
What's the plan? Hey, Ango--

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:42.340
At all times, the most important thing is
to have situational awareness.

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:46.550
Where are you? What's nearby?

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:50.140
How much time do you have?
What are your priorities?

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:52.270
What can you use?

00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:57.860
Arashi. I'm throwing you a rope.

00:12:58.190 --> 00:12:59.440
Tie it around the both of you.

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:01.280
-Right.
-Right.

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:03.110
Both of us together?

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.450
Right! Do you know how to tie it off?

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:06.410
I think so.

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:08.410
Both at once is impossible!

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:11.490
Semimaru, take the end of the rope
and don't let go.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:14.580
<i>How many supports can I make
with the tools on hand?</i>

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:16.330
<i>How much weight will it hold?</i>

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:21.340
<i>It's a reinforced rope. Including clothes
and bags, they weigh just over 110 kilos.</i>

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:24.920
Semimaru, help me out.
We'll push this off.

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:26.300
-What?
-Hurry up!

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:27.470
Okay!

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:30.220
Hold on! Wait a second!

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:31.970
Won't this break the rope?

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:33.100
I don't know.

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:34.270
You don't know?

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:37.520
It would take too long to pull them up
by hand one by one this far.

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:39.900
They're here!

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:43.730
Ango, we're all set!
The bacteria have started to come in!

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:46.610
Shit! We have no choice! Ready, go!

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:57.040
It's not falling!

00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:59.000
Should I cut it with my knife?

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:01.590
Don't be stupid!
It will shock you if it's electrified!

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:05.970
Ango, at the very least, pull Natsu up!

00:14:07.170 --> 00:14:08.470
<i>He cares about me!</i>

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:10.180
<i>But it doesn't make me happy.</i>

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:12.050
<i>Even as close as we are now!</i>

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:15.020
<i>It just sounds like he's saying,
"I'll die here to be with Hana."</i>

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:16.230
Hey, Ango!

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:19.770
I wanted to reduce the impact on them,
so this is perfect.

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:34.540
Semimaru! Pull them up!

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:36.660
I would, but I can't reach it!

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:37.750
Ango!

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:38.870
Ryochin!

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:43.630
Take this rope
and wrap it around yourselves.

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:44.920
Make sure you won't slip out!

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:46.920
Okay!

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:50.680
-Arashi, you have your knife, right?
-Yes!

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:52.180
Cut the first rope.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:54.180
Semimaru, come help us pull them.

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:55.140
Right!

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:57.430
-Natsu, grit your teeth.
-Okay.

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:02.230
Pull them up!

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:07.780
<i>They're eating up
the equipment we dropped.</i>

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:10.650
<i>It's like they're sentient predators.</i>

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:15.990
Fine, I'll give you some food.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:31.760
<i>What do you think will be
most important in the future?</i>

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:34.220
Attentiveness and good judgment.

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:36.510
Decisiveness and the will to act.

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:40.020
You already have all of those things.

00:15:40.730 --> 00:15:43.480
We don't have time to rest.
We need to hurry and go up.

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:51.400
Welcome back, everyone.

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:54.870
Ms. Botan and Matsuri, do you read me?

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:56.120
<i>Everyone made it back!</i>

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:57.410
Thank goodness!

00:15:57.490 --> 00:15:58.990
We've found a way out here too.

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:00.200
Come quick!

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:01.210
Let's move.

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:03.420
Thank you.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:06.290
I'm sorry for being selfish.

00:16:08.340 --> 00:16:09.250
Thanks.

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:10.710
No thanks necessary.

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:12.630
I like to avoid sink or swim situations.

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:18.140
<i>Back at that moment, why didn't I do
everything I could to rescue Hana?</i>

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:22.020
That was pretty reckless of you.

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:23.890
There were no other options.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:26.860
Thank you.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:28.110
I didn't do anything.

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:30.030
Save it for Ango and Ryo.

00:16:30.690 --> 00:16:33.650
<i>I couldn't do a thing. Not a damn thing.</i>

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:38.370
<i>In that brief moment, while I was
just sitting there spacing out,</i>

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:41.120
<i>those guys managed to accomplish
so much more.</i>

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:43.710
Thank you.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:45.540
It wasn't a waste.

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:47.880
It wasn't a waste at all.

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:50.960
<i>He's right.</i>

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:53.380
<i>What we learned there wasn't a waste.</i>

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:57.640
What a relief! Except, we didn't stop
the missiles, so it's not all good.

00:16:58.390 --> 00:17:01.720
So, have you started to
trust Ryo a little, Ms. Botan?

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:06.100
I was kind of happy when you asked him
to go back to save Nat and Arashi.

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:07.350
I suppose.

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.440
Oh, here they come.

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:11.070
Hey, over here!

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:14.490
An exit! I can see stars up there!

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:19.580
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:21.740
We couldn't stop the launch.

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:24.160
I wanted to stop it more than anything.

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.580
No point fretting over it!

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:27.370
We did everything we could have.

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:29.880
You wanted to stop them
for Hana's sake, right?

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:30.960
That's one reason.

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:33.380
But I also wanted to do it
for the other teams.

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:35.010
And most importantly,

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:36.510
for my own sake.

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:38.970
I want to live here.

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:42.010
I want to continue living in this world

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:43.810
along with all of you.

00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:51.320
That's why I'm begging you,
please stop all of the missiles!

00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:52.360
Please!

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:54.400
Who are you even asking?

00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:56.150
Let's go. We don't have time.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:59.360
Right now, we need to
get everyone out safely

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:01.950
and evacuate these waters
before time runs out.

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:03.370
That's our only option.

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:16.880
<i>Please stop it!
I have no idea who I'm even praying to.</i>

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:18.800
<i>But please just stop it.</i>

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:23.470
<i>Right now,
everyone has someone on their minds.</i>

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:27.270
<i>Hibari...</i>

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:35.690
<i>The missiles may rain down
on the others we separated from.</i>

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:46.410
Are you okay?

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:47.410
Yes.

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:54.840
It stopped?

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:55.800
What?

00:18:55.880 --> 00:18:57.840
That monitor's probably just busted.

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:00.260
No, it also stopped on that one.

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:04.510
The power!

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:11.310
All the lights are going out.

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:16.570
The ship's power died, which means
the missile launch stopped too.

00:19:17.110 --> 00:19:18.740
What? But why?

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:24.370
The bacteria?

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:27.620
That makes sense.
I even said it a few times myself.

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:31.040
I said that the bacteria
could interfere with the ship's systems.

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:33.460
It's the bacteria
that stopped the missiles.

00:19:40.420 --> 00:19:42.470
Natsu, I'm sure it was thanks to you.

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:43.390
What?

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:46.470
The bacteria spread around
because you walked all over the ship.

00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:52.900
The rest of us were
just making a ruckus. Amazing.

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:56.690
Don't you think it's crazy
just how amazing living creatures can be?

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:59.230
So, what is this bacteria
you guys are going on about?

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:00.280
Didn't you see it?

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:06.280
We're out!

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:08.290
-Hooray! We made it!
-We're outside!

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:11.870
Fresh air.

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:37.060
Hey, Ryo.

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:41.990
Don't you feel that, just a little bit,
it was a good thing we came here?

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:46.200
See? The difference between good
and bad things is often hard to tell.

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:48.830
After all,
they usually happen in the same place.

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:51.580
<i>I see. This isn't a test.</i>

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:54.790
<i>An artificial test is
far from what happens in reality.</i>

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:57.500
<i>In the end, a test is just a test.</i>

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:01.170
<i>And reality is definitely not a test.</i>

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:03.840
Ryo.

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:11.720
Regardless of what may come,
I will never use this.

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:19.980
All right. Let's get going.

00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:13.800
<i>Hana, how are you?</i>

00:23:16.220 --> 00:23:18.770
<i>I would really like to introduce you
to everyone here.</i>

00:23:20.270 --> 00:23:21.600
<i>Let's keep on living together...</i>

00:23:22.310 --> 00:23:23.520
<i>in this world.</i>

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:31.070
<i>Arashi, what are you up to?</i>

00:23:32.070 --> 00:23:35.910
<i>At first, I thought that I could never
live in a world like this.</i>

00:23:36.490 --> 00:23:38.290
<i>But I've made up my mind.</i>

00:23:41.460 --> 00:23:46.040
<i>I'm going to live on here in this world.</i>
